  <iati-identifier>GB-CHC-285776-SUD263</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="GB-CHC-285776" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Western Equatoria State Recovery, Reintegration and Sustainable Livelihoods Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a 5 years project for communities in Western Equatoria State.  The project will provide agricultural seeds and tools, extension services, access to markets, support to small scale businesses and value addition to locally available natural resources such as honey processing. The project will specifically target 1000 PLWHAs, 1000 small holder farmers and 1000 with livestock restocking, and non-farm related activities.  IDPs and Refugees will also directly benefit from this project. The project will generally increase agricultural yield, create access to markets and diversify livelihoods strategies for 3000 households.  An agriculture accompanier will be seconded by Caritas Austria to provide technical support during the project implementation and will work closely with Diocesan Livelihoods Programme Coordinator, field officers and extension workers.  The project will also be closely coordinated with Western Equatoria State Ministry of Agriculture, and the County and Payam authorities at the local level.</narrative>
  </description>
